# Computer Use AI SDK Integration Guide

## Overview
The Juno AI Computer Use Agent leverages the [computer-use-ai-sdk](mdc:src-tauri/mcp-server-os-level) for native desktop automation capabilities. This guide covers proper integration patterns and API usage.

## SDK Architecture

### Core Components
- **[Desktop](mdc:src-tauri/mcp-server-os-level/src/lib.rs)**: Main entry point for desktop automation
- **[UIElement](mdc:src-tauri/mcp-server-os-level/src/element.rs)**: Represents UI elements with interaction capabilities
- **[Locator](mdc:src-tauri/mcp-server-os-level/src/locator.rs)**: High-level API for finding and interacting with elements
- **[Selector](mdc:src-tauri/mcp-server-os-level/src/selector.rs)**: Element selection patterns
- **[AccessibilityEngine](mdc:src-tauri/mcp-server-os-level/src/platforms)**: Platform-specific accessibility implementations

### Platform Support
- **macOS**: Full native accessibility support via [macos/engine.rs](mdc:src-tauri/mcp-server-os-level/src/platforms/macos/engine.rs)
- **Other Platforms**: Limited support, graceful degradation

## Basic Usage Patterns

### Desktop Initialization
```rust
use computer_use_ai_sdk::{Desktop, AutomationError};

// Standard initialization
let desktop = Desktop::new(true, true)?; // use_background_apps, activate_app

// With auto-redirect for permission handling
let desktop = Desktop::new_with_auto_redirect(true, true, false)?; // auto_open_settings
```

### Element Discovery
```rust
// Get all applications
let applications = desktop.applications()?;

// Find specific application
let app = desktop.application("Safari")?;

// Get focused element
let focused = desktop.focused_element()?;

// Use locator for element discovery
let locator = app.locator("button")?;
let buttons = locator.all()?; // Get all matching elements
let first_button = locator.first()?; // Get first match
```

### Element Interaction
```rust
// Basic interactions
element.click()?;
element.double_click()?;
element.right_click()?;
element.type_text("Hello, World!")?;

// Element properties
let bounds = element.bounds()?; // (x, y, width, height)
let attributes = element.attributes();
let is_enabled = element.is_enabled()?;
let is_visible = element.is_visible()?;

// Element hierarchy
let children = element.children()?;
let parent = element.parent()?;
```

### Selector Patterns
```rust
use computer_use_ai_sdk::Selector;

// Role-based selection
let buttons = app.locator("button")?;

// Complex selectors (when available)
let text_fields = app.locator("textfield")?;
let checkboxes = app.locator("checkbox")?;

// Universal selector
let all_elements = app.locator("*")?;
```

## Integration Best Practices

### Error Handling
```rust
use computer_use_ai_sdk::AutomationError;

match desktop.application("NonExistentApp") {
    Ok(app) => {
        // Handle success
    }
    Err(AutomationError::NotFound(msg)) => {
        // Application not found
    }
    Err(AutomationError::PermissionDenied(msg)) => {
        // Accessibility permissions required
    }
    Err(e) => {
        // Other errors
    }
}
```

### Async Integration
```rust
// SDK methods are sync, wrap for async contexts
async fn find_elements_async(app: &UIElement) -> Result<Vec<UIElement>, String> {
    tokio::task::spawn_blocking({
        let app = app.clone();
        move || {
            let locator = app.locator("*").map_err(|e| e.to_string())?;
            locator.all().map_err(|e| e.to_string())
        }
    })
    .await
    .map_err(|e| format!("Task join error: {}", e))?
}
```

### Thread Safety
```rust
use std::sync::{Arc, Mutex};

// Desktop is Clone and thread-safe
#[derive(Clone)]
pub struct DesktopWrapper {
    desktop: Arc<Mutex<Option<Desktop>>>,
}

impl DesktopWrapper {
    pub fn new() -> Self {
        Self {
            desktop: Arc::new(Mutex::new(None)),
        }
    }

    pub fn ensure_initialized(&self) -> Result<(), String> {
        let mut guard = self.desktop.lock().map_err(|e| e.to_string())?;
        if guard.is_none() {
            let desktop = Desktop::new_with_auto_redirect(true, true, false)
                .map_err(|e| e.to_string())?;
            *guard = Some(desktop);
        }
        Ok(())
    }
}
```

## Advanced Patterns

### Element Caching
```rust
use std::collections::HashMap;

pub struct ElementCache {
    elements: Arc<Mutex<HashMap<u32, UIElement>>>,
    next_id: Arc<Mutex<u32>>,
}

impl ElementCache {
    pub fn cache_element(&self, element: UIElement) -> Result<u32, String> {
        let mut elements = self.elements.lock().map_err(|e| e.to_string())?;
        let mut next_id = self.next_id.lock().map_err(|e| e.to_string())?;

        let id = *next_id;
        *next_id += 1;

        elements.insert(id, element);
        Ok(id)
    }

    pub fn get_element(&self, id: u32) -> Result<Option<UIElement>, String> {
        let elements = self.elements.lock().map_err(|e| e.to_string())?;
        Ok(elements.get(&id).cloned())
    }
}
```

### Permission Handling
```rust
pub fn check_accessibility_permissions(desktop: &Desktop) -> Result<bool, String> {
    // Try a simple operation to test permissions
    match desktop.applications() {
        Ok(_) => Ok(true),
        Err(AutomationError::PermissionDenied(_)) => Ok(false),
        Err(e) => Err(format!("Permission check failed: {}", e)),
    }
}

pub async fn ensure_permissions_with_retry(desktop: &Desktop) -> Result<(), String> {
    for attempt in 1..=3 {
        match check_accessibility_permissions(desktop) {
            Ok(true) => return Ok(()),
            Ok(false) => {
                if attempt == 3 {
                    return Err("Accessibility permissions required".to_string());
                }
                // Wait and retry
                tokio::time::sleep(tokio::time::Duration::from_secs(1)).await;
            }
            Err(e) => return Err(e),
        }
    }
    Err("Permission check timeout".to_string())
}
```

### Application-Specific Patterns
```rust
pub struct SafariAutomation {
    desktop: Desktop,
}

impl SafariAutomation {
    pub fn new() -> Result<Self, AutomationError> {
        let desktop = Desktop::new_with_auto_redirect(true, true, false)?;
        Ok(Self { desktop })
    }

    pub fn get_safari_app(&self) -> Result<UIElement, AutomationError> {
        // Try to find Safari, open if not found
        match self.desktop.application("Safari") {
            Ok(app) => Ok(app),
            Err(AutomationError::NotFound(_)) => {
                // Open Safari and wait
                self.desktop.open_application("Safari")
            }
            Err(e) => Err(e),
        }
    }

    pub fn get_web_content(&self) -> Result<Vec<UIElement>, AutomationError> {
        let safari = self.get_safari_app()?;
        let locator = safari.locator("webarea")?;
        locator.all()
    }
}
```

## Common Patterns

### Element Filtering
```rust
pub fn filter_clickable_elements(elements: Vec<UIElement>) -> Vec<UIElement> {
    elements
        .into_iter()
        .filter(|element| {
            // Check if element is clickable
            let attributes = element.attributes();
            matches!(
                attributes.role.as_str(),
                "button" | "link" | "textfield" | "checkbox" | "radiobutton"
                | "popupbutton" | "tab" | "menuitem" | "image" | "cell"
            )
        })
        .filter(|element| {
            // Check if element has reasonable size
            if let Ok((_, _, width, height)) = element.bounds() {
                width >= 5.0 && height >= 5.0
            } else {
                false
            }
        })
        .filter(|element| {
            // Check if element has useful text
            let attributes = element.attributes();
            attributes.label.is_some() || attributes.description.is_some()
        })
        .collect()
}
```

### Robust Element Access
```rust
pub fn safe_element_operation<F, T>(element: &UIElement, operation: F) -> Result<T, String>
where
    F: FnOnce(&UIElement) -> Result<T, AutomationError>,
{
    // Check if element is still valid
    if !element.is_enabled().unwrap_or(false) {
        return Err("Element is not enabled".to_string());
    }

    if !element.is_visible().unwrap_or(false) {
        return Err("Element is not visible".to_string());
    }

    // Perform operation with error handling
    operation(element).map_err(|e| match e {
        AutomationError::NotFound(_) => "Element no longer exists".to_string(),
        AutomationError::PermissionDenied(_) => "Permission denied for operation".to_string(),
        AutomationError::Timeout(_) => "Operation timed out".to_string(),
        _ => format!("Operation failed: {}", e),
    })
}
```

## Debugging and Logging

### Element Inspection
```rust
pub fn debug_element(element: &UIElement) -> String {
    let attributes = element.attributes();
    let bounds = element.bounds().unwrap_or((0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0));

    format!(
        "Element[role={}, label={:?}, bounds=({:.1}, {:.1}, {:.1}, {:.1})]",
        attributes.role,
        attributes.label,
        bounds.0, bounds.1, bounds.2, bounds.3
    )
}

pub fn log_element_hierarchy(element: &UIElement, depth: usize) {
    let indent = "  ".repeat(depth);
    println!("{}{}", indent, debug_element(element));

    if let Ok(children) = element.children() {
        for child in children {
            log_element_hierarchy(&child, depth + 1);
        }
    }
}
```

## Error Recovery

### Graceful Degradation
```rust
pub fn try_desktop_operation<F, T>(operation: F) -> Result<T, String>
where
    F: FnOnce() -> Result<T, AutomationError>,
{
    match operation() {
        Ok(result) => Ok(result),
        Err(AutomationError::PermissionDenied(_)) => {
            Err("Accessibility permissions required. Please enable in System Settings.".to_string())
        }
        Err(AutomationError::NotFound(msg)) => {
            Err(format!("Element not found: {}", msg))
        }
        Err(AutomationError::Timeout(msg)) => {
            Err(format!("Operation timed out: {}", msg))
        }
        Err(e) => {
            Err(format!("Desktop operation failed: {}", e))
        }
    }
}
```

## Performance Considerations

### Lazy Initialization
- Initialize Desktop only when needed
- Cache Desktop instance for reuse
- Use spawn_blocking for CPU-intensive operations

### Memory Management
- UIElement implements Clone efficiently
- Clear element caches periodically
- Avoid holding large element collections

### Operation Timing
- Most operations are fast (< 100ms)
- Element discovery can be slower for complex UIs
- Use timeouts for operations that might hang

